WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.130
An easy English sentence:
Young people like music.

2
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:05.790
Four short words.

3
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.740
In French, it comes out as
«Les jeunes aiment la musique».

4
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.170
Count the tiles.

5
00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:15.020
French has slipped in small
words that English never wrote.

6
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.470
Where do they come from?

7
00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.600
And that was one short line.

8
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.760
So how do you turn a whole English passage

9
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.300
into French without tripping
over every small word?

10
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.990
In this mission, you'll take English
sentences apart in Mission D1,

11
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.510
and light up the trigger
board in Mission D2.

12
00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.350
Then you'll build a full passage,

13
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:37.410
line by line, and climb the
check ladder in Mission D3.

14
00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.630
Your mission: find out
where the small words hide,

15
00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.530
and build French that holds up.
